  "key_scientific_findings": {
    "empirical_grid_robustness": "On the primary 24-race benchmark, Empirical Grid achieves 1.8535 log loss and 0.0084 Brier, outperforming Frozen Model A (2.2907 log loss, p=0.038) and Remediated Model B (2.2831 log loss, p=0.035). When evaluated across all objective pre-race categories (dry vs wet, low vs high penalties, with or without pit starts), Empirical Grid remains superior or competitive across every single pre-race objective subset. ML models do NOT beat the empirical baseline even in disrupted races.",
    "methodological_cherry_picking_warning": "Removing outlier races post-hoc (such as Miami or Interlagos) drastically inflates perceived accuracy (dropping log loss to 1.368), but is scientifically invalid because extreme outcomes are intrinsic to motorsport. The complete season must remain the governing ground truth."
  }
